  "note": "Codified from the City of Buda Unified Development Code (UDC), Section 2.07 'Zoning Dimensional Regulations' — the two consolidated dimensional tables (Residential Dimensional Regulations and Nonresidential Dimensional Regulations). Source is eCode360 (General Code). Side yard is stated as Interior/Corner; side_ft = interior, side_corner_ft = corner. Buda states BOTH Maximum Building Coverage (%) and Maximum Impervious Cover (%) explicitly, so both fields are ordinance-sourced (unlike Dripping Springs and Kyle, whose codes specify only one coverage figure). The UDC notes that impervious cover and building coverage 'may be altered elsewhere in this UDC depending on a property's particular' overlay/PUD; per-parcel overrides are not modeled here. P-258 LANE-C ADDENDUM (2026-09-16, acquisition campaign, branch seat/p258-lane-c): 4 districts added to the NONRESIDENTIAL table this file only half-copied before -- B-2 Arterial Business, B-3 Interstate-35 Business, LI Light Industrial and HI Heavy Industrial -- from the same page this file already cites (eCode360 Subsection 2.07 Zoning Dimensional Regulations, https://ecode360.com/40956702, read 2026-09-16). The pre-existing rows cover 2.07.01 (residential: AG, R-1, R-2, R-3, R-4, R-5, R-MH) and B-1 only; 2.07.02's five nonresidential columns (B-1, B-2, B-3, LI, HI) had been left at one. Values: B-2 F40/S0-25/R35/H45/BC50/IC80; B-3 F50/S0-30/R40/H45/BC40/IC75; LI F40/S0-25/R35/H45/BC60/IC75; HI F50/S0-20/R30/H35/BC65/IC75. Buda states interior and corner side separately and states BOTH building coverage and impervious coverage, so side_ft = interior, side_corner_ft = corner, and both coverage fields are ordinance-sourced. NOT ROWED, WITH EVIDENCE -- THE FORM DISTRICTS (F1, F2, F3, F3H, F4, F4H, F5, F5H; 449 of this city's lane-c parcels, the largest single block): these are NOT Euclidean districts with a per-district setback row. Subsection 2.05.05 states there are eight form districts and that each has corresponding regulations; the dimensional standards live in the FORM BASED CODE, Subsection 2.08, keyed by BUILDING TYPE and by street type (Section D Promenade Street F4/F5/F5H; Section E Community Connector F3/F4/F4H/F5/F5H; Section F Active Street F4/F5/F5H; Section G Neighborhood Connector F4/F4H/F5/F5H; Section H Neighborhood Local Street F1/F3/F3H/F4/F4H), with F2 Reserved. A single scalar front/side/rear row would misrepresent every one of them, so no row is written; the citation is Subsection 2.05.05 (intent and district roster, read this pass at https://ecode360.com/40956517) and Subsection 2.08 (Form Based Code standards, cited not transcribed) plus the City-published UDC update PDF at https://www.budatx.gov/DocumentCenter/View/8865/2021-10-UDC-Update. Recorded BLOCKED, not guessed. ALSO NOT ROWED: the layer code 'B2/R5' (4 parcels) is a COMPOUND code -- it names two districts at once and no single row can honestly answer it; it does NOT fall to the conservative fallback: under the envelope's mapDistrict contract the normalized code 'B2R5' PREFIX-matches the 'B-2' row (isSafePrefixMatch, shorter token at least 2 chars) and resolves to B-2 at confidence 0.7, so the R-5 half of the parcel's code is silently ignored. That is a real 4-parcel alignment defect for the layer (or a per-parcel read) to fix, and the earlier sentence in this same addendum claiming it would fall to the conservative fallback was WRONG -- corrected here and in the P-258 lane-c fragment. Recorded BLOCKED with this note as the evidence.",
